  "notes": "{垂|た}らす has two core meanings: letting liquid fall in drops, and letting something hang down loosely.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{垂|た}れる→垂れる：10075_tareru⟧ (intransitive, to drip/hang down)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{垂|た}らしている describes an ongoing action (dripping) or a maintained state (dangling).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{醤油|しょうゆ}→醤油：01056_shouyu⟧を{垂|た}らす: to drizzle soy sauce\n- ⟦よだれ→よだれ：09087_yodare⟧を{垂|た}らす: to drool\n- ⟦{足|あし}→足：00575_ashi⟧を{垂|た}らす: to dangle one's feet\n- ⟦{糸|いと}→糸：01315_ito⟧を{垂|た}らす: to let a line hang down (fishing)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n⟦よだれ→よだれ：09087_yodare⟧を{垂|た}らす can figuratively mean to covet something eagerly.",
